{
  "dom_id": "step-34985",
  "name": "Extending the Sums of Angles Rule",
  "problem": "We can extend our rule relating sums of adjacent angles to more than two angles.\n\nFor example, let's consider the angles shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/3264d0ab1a40b02915a737dad57e9f26820193d9bdc6b42431ec1ab6508cc523.png)\n\nAccording to our rule, the measure of the reflex angle $\\angle QST$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QST & ={{m∠QSP}_{⏟}}_{\\text{green angle}}+{{m∠PSR}_{⏟}}_{\\text{orange angle}}+{{m∠RST}_{⏟}}_{\\text{blue angle}} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}+{95}^{∘}+{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={240}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can also use this rule to determine the size of a smaller angle when we know a larger one. Let's see an example.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
